def find_longest_repeating_subseq(s):
    n = len(s)
    # Create a 2D array to store lengths of longest common suffixes
    lcs_length = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]

    # Build the lcs_length table
    for i in range(1, n + 1):
        for j in range(1, n + 1):
            if s[i - 1] == s[j - 1]:
                lcs_length[i][j] = lcs_length[i - 1][j - 1] + 1
            else:
                lcs_length[i][j] = max(lcs_length[i - 1][j], lcs_length[i][j - 1])

    # The length of the longest repeating subsequence is the value in the bottom-right corner of the table
    return lcs_length[n][n]
```

The `find_longest_repeating_subseq` function uses dynamic programming to build a 2D array `lcs_length` where `lcs_length[i][j]` represents the length of the longest common suffix of the substrings `s[0..i-1]` and `s[0..j-1]`. The function iterates through each character of the string, comparing it with all previous characters to update the `lcs_length` table accordingly. Finally, the length of the longest repeating subsequence is found in `lcs_length[n][n]`, which corresponds to the entire string.

