def max_sum(arr, n):
    # Initialize the dp arrays for increasing and decreasing subsequences
    inc = [1] * n
    dec = [1] * n

    # Build the increasing subsequences
    for i in range(1, n):
        for j in range(i):
            if arr[i] > arr[j]:
                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + 1)

    # Build the decreasing subsequences
    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):
        for j in range(i+1, n):
            if arr[i] > arr[j]:
                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + 1)

    # Find the maximum sum of bi-tonic sub-sequence
    max_sum = 0
    for i in range(n):
        max_sum = max(max_sum, inc[i] + dec[i] - 1)

    return max_sum
```

This function uses dynamic programming to build two arrays: `inc` for increasing subsequences and `dec` for decreasing subsequences. It then calculates the maximum sum of bi-tonic sub-sequences by considering all possible starting points and ending points of the subsequences. The final result is the maximum sum found among all bi-tonic subsequences.

